The best (and, for the purposes of this post, accepted) theory of Eye
of the Aethiopica's nomenclature is that "the Aethiopica" refers to
_Threskiornis aethiopicus_, also known as the Sacred Ibis. Thus the
reasoning behind its name is:
Aethiopica (scientific name of...) -> Ibis (animal form of...) -> Thoth
(god of magic).

But!

Its name was decided in v3.1.0. Since then, the wizard class has
changed to permit Chaotic supplicants. As a result, the Wizard of
Balance's name was changed. But, owing to the obscurity of the
reasoning behind The Eye of the Aethiopica's moniker, its name remains
unchanged.

And, as a result, wizards loyal to Anhur (chaotic) can acquire what is
by definition an artifact of Thoth (neutral). This isn't very good.

However, the possibilities for a replacement name for an artifact that
confers Energy (mana) Regeneration and Opens Portals when invoked are
slim. One could consider The Eye of Horus as a fitting candidate, but
the powers of The Eye of Horus are strictly related to healing and
returning from the dead. (Indeed, if the Eye of Horus ever did get made
into an artifact, it would have to be an artifact Amulet of Life
Saving. How's that for a YANI?)

Does anyone have any ideas? Preferably names which are not made up, if
you please.



